2026-10-02T23:50:53.714987Z TRACE codex_api::sse::responses: SSE event: {"type":"response.output_text.done","content_index":0,"item_id":"msg_[REDACTED]","logprobs":[],"output_index":0,"sequence_number":648,"text":"**Found one remaining evidence-loss path:** an object-shaped completion event with a missing or null `response` throws before raw tapes are attached.\n\nVerified the six inspected parser/consumer files match tree `7072895a8cac96ca9fd0f9d1ad6ab56356fe8117` byte for byte. Citations below refer to that snapshot under `trai_brain/mercury-bridge/`.\n\nA concrete input sequence is:\n\n```text\nstdout:\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"Actual review answer\"}}\n{\"type\":\"turn.completed\"}\n\nstderr:\nSSE event: {\"type\":\"response.completed\",\"response\":null}\n```\n\nThe source establishes this path:\n\n1. `codex-challenger.js:48-56` accepts the SSE object and includes it in `completed`. The observations filter skips its null `response`.\n2. `codex-challenger.js:89-92` successfully extracts the actual answer.\n3. **`codex-challenger.js:148` dereferences `event.response.model`**, throwing a `TypeError`. This occurs before raw buffers are attached at line 160 or the answer is returned at line 168. No surrounding catch attaches `providerMetadata`.\n4. Preflight’s catch therefore constructs fallback metadata without tapes (`provider-preflight.js:206-217`). Its persistence helper writes an empty stdout buffer and omits stderr (`provider-preflight.js:143-161`).\n5. The stage consumer likewise falls back to metadata without tapes and persists empty stdout/no stderr (`adversarial-review.js:1146-1163`). The outer review returns a failure receipt without the captured answer (`adversarial-review.js:1235-1244,1350-1379`).\n\nThis produces an explicit failure, **but loses the captured answer and both tapes from the receipt path**. The finding is the lost evidence, not the existence of a parse diagnostic.\n\n**Introduced versus existing:** `codex-challenger.js` is newly added relative to base `3afde60ce654ec191a6a73413bb5ab5cf8acf6d1`; its unguarded completion dereference introduces this producer path. The consumers’ fallback behavior already existed. This is a residual hole in the corrected adapter, not evidence that the new top-level frame guards themselves caused a regression.\n\n**Mercury’s stated mechanism is unsupported.** Excluding malformed values from structured arrays does not discard their raw tapes: the normal path attaches both buffers and consumers persist them. Moreover, `classifyFableFallbackError` requires Claude/Fable provenance (`adversarial-review.js:904-917,996-1007`), and the actual Astra dispatch does not call it (`adversarial-review.js:1220-1242`).\n\nCoverage: static inspection of parsing, metadata construction, preflight, stage receipt persistence, identity/fallback routing, and relevant base differences. No tests, provider calls, mutations, or runtime changes. The malformed completion is a concrete source-level input counterexample; I did not establish that the live provider has emitted it."}
